Step 4: Configure .env File
Open NexApply.Api/.env and replace the placeholder values:

# Database
ConnectionStrings__DefaultConnection=Host=localhost;Port=5432;Database=NextApplyDb;Username=postgres;Password=YOUR_PASSWORD

# JWT (Generate random 64-char string)
AppSettings__Token=YOUR_GENERATED_TOKEN_HERE
AppSettings__Issuer=NexApply
AppSettings__Audience=NexApplyUsers

# Google OAuth (Get from Google Cloud Console)
Authentication__Google__ClientId=YOUR_CLIENT_ID.apps.googleusercontent.com
Authentication__Google__ClientSecret=YOUR_CLIENT_SECRET

# Email (Gmail App Password)
EmailSettings__SmtpHost=smtp.gmail.com
EmailSettings__SmtpPort=587
EmailSettings__SmtpUsername=your-email@gmail.com
EmailSettings__SmtpPassword=your-16-char-app-password
EmailSettings__FromEmail=your-email@gmail.com
EmailSettings__FromName=NexApply


Copy
Step 5: Generate JWT Secret
# Windows PowerShell
-join ((65..90) + (97..122) + (48..57) | Get-Random -Count 64 | ForEach-Object {[char]$_})

# macOS/Linux
openssl rand -base64 64 | tr -d '\n'

Copy
pow
Copy the output and paste into AppSettings__Token

Step 6: Setup Google OAuth
Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/

Create project → Enable Google+ API

Credentials → Create OAuth 2.0 Client ID

Add redirect URI: https://localhost:7001/api/auth/google-callback

Copy Client ID & Secret to .env

Step 7: Setup Gmail App Password
Go to https://myaccount.google.com/security

Enable 2-Step Verification

App passwords → Mail → Other → "NexApply"

Copy 16-char password to .env (remove spaces)

Step 8: Setup Database
# Create database
psql -U postgres
CREATE DATABASE NextApplyDb;
\q

# Apply migrations
dotnet ef database update

