⚠️ Important Notes
Never commit .env file (already in .gitignore)

Use double underscores __ for nested config

No spaces around = in .env file

Minimum 32 characters for JWT token

Troubleshooting
Issue	Solution
"Configuration not found"	Ensure .env is in NexApply.Api/ folder
"Database connection failed"	Check PostgreSQL is running & credentials correct
"JWT token invalid"	Token must be 32+ characters
"Google OAuth error"	Verify redirect URI matches exactly
"Email failed"	Use App Password, not regular Gmail password
Production Deployment
Use platform environment variables instead of .env:

Azure App Service:
Configuration → Application settings → Add variables

Docker:

docker run -e ConnectionStrings__DefaultConnection="..." nexapply-api

Copy
bash
Docker Compose:

environment:
  - ConnectionStrings__DefaultConnection=...
  - AppSettings__Token=...

